course: dictionary
lesson: 11502
title: Agreeable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Agreeable is a word for something or someone that is pleasant and nice. «The afternoon was warm and agreeable, so we sat in the park.» Warm and sitting in the park sound nice, so agreeable means pleasant.
explain: Agreeable can also describe a person. «Our new neighbour is very agreeable and always says hello.» The clue is always says hello, which is friendly. Agreeable means friendly and easy to get on with. Check by swapping in nice: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Agreeable can mean willing to say yes. «We asked if we could stay up late, and Dad was agreeable.» Dad did not say no, so he was willing. In formal talk, it can mean acceptable to people: «Is that plan agreeable to everyone?»
fact: «Agreeable» means pleasant and nice.
fact: «Agreeable» can mean friendly and easy to get on with, or willing to agree to something.
fact: In formal talk, «agreeable» means acceptable to people: «Is that agreeable to everyone?»
fact: Useful phrases: «agreeable to», «an agreeable surprise», «perfectly agreeable».
fact: Agreeable comes from agree, so a good way to remember its meaning is to think of someone who is ready to say yes.
exercise: «The afternoon was warm and agreeable, so we sat in the park.» What does agreeable mean here? | Noisy and busy | *Pleasant and nice | Empty and dark | Unpleasant and cold
exercise: Mia said, «I'm happy to help, I'm agreeable.» Which meaning fits best? | Loud | Heavy | Painful | *Willing to agree
exercise: Choose the word that fits: «It was an ___ surprise to find a birthday cake under the table.» | treacherous | curt | ancient | *agreeable
test: «Our new neighbour is very agreeable and always says hello.» What does agreeable mean? | Cold and wet | Very old | Angry and loud | *Friendly and easy to get on with
test: «Is that plan agreeable to everyone?» In this sentence, agreeable means? | Dangerous | Expensive | Tasty | *Acceptable to people
exam: «Dad was agreeable when we asked to stay up late.» Which word is closest in meaning to agreeable here? | *Willing | Silent | Tired | Rude
